findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) can opener blade (food debris/paper) - ran through dish machine during inspection;
B) fry baskets (grease/food debris); 
C) metal baffle inside ice machine (buildup along lower edge);  and
D) soda gun/holder at banquet area bar (buildup) .

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use (for in-use items such as the can opener), to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) inside kitchen fridge/freezer unit by 3 part sink (splash/debris in the bottom of both sections);
B) under coffee and tea makers in banquet area (dust/debris);
C) outer surfaces of cabinets under coffee and tea maker in banquet area (splash); 
D) speed rail at bar in banquet area (splash/debris);
E) motor compartment of unused keg cooler at bar in banquet area and general surfaces around it (old mouse droppings);
F) lower compartment on the back side of salad bar unit in banquet area (old mouse droppings);
G) in furnace closet (old mouse droppings);
H) walkin cooler shelves (general buildup); 
I) inside keg cooler at bar (general buildup);   and
J) lower shelves in kitchen dry storage room (old mouse droppings).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
